description:
{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Dark Elf
|race       = Human
|number     = 454
}}

One of Hess's Eight Sages. It was sealed away in the water crystal after the great war 700 years ago. Though set free when the crystal was destroyed, seemingly due to being restrained for so long under such power he lost his sense of judgement, and became overcome by his destructive urges. His power is befitting that of Hess's Eight Sages, with the massive magic attacks he unleashes boasting devastating force.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Orthros
|race       = Aquatic
|number     = 461
}}

A gigantic octopus monster from a faraway world. It is known for its purple body and sharp teeth. In the Farplane where the stories of espers and humans intertwine, on top of understanding human speech it speaks its own strange dialect, and is said to have stood before many a soldier who tried taking on the empire. It is capable of many octopus-like attacks including tentacle and ink. It also appears to look up to the gale-manipulating typhon as a sort of teacher.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Marie
|race       = Human
|number     = 503
}}

The vision of a green mage that no longer exists as summoned by Sakura. Marie was a green mage hailing from Mysidia who specialized in using her unique skills to bolster her allies and cripple her enemies. Although she was considered to be one of the greatest green mages in the nation, a darker side of her personality manifested itself in her obsession with her research. Rumor has it that she was always patiently eager to see the result of her enfeebling magic on her enemies.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Gluttony
|race       = Demon
|number     = 646
}}

A demon that eats everything it sees using the gigantic mouth located on its stomach. It is the altered spirit of desire form taken by greedy humans who used a certain secret technique. No matter how much they eat, their hunger is never satiated, so their pangs never end. Oddly enough, they seem to enjoy that. Because they hold memories of when they were human, they can make intelligent decisions, which makes them quite difficult to face. It will use any means available so long as it can satisfy its never-ending hunger.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Great Malboro
|race       = Plant
|number     = 1090
}}

An unusually shaped monster with a giant mouth and tentacles. The breath it breathes is infused with poison that it holds within its body. It is said that even if all the poisons in existence were put together it wouldn't come close to the virulence of the great malboro's poison. Its breath is so foul that it can be detected a mile away. A certain researcher has theorized that most of the poison in the world now were born from the great malboro's poison.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Forelsket
|race       = Human
|number     = 1150
}}

An elven chef that lives deep in the forest. He uses a giant butcher's knife, and wanders various areas in search of ingredients, but his actions and looks make him seem more like a trespasser than a chef. Leopold and Magna was with Forelsket, but they feared they were next on Forelsket's menu, so they decide to run away, and as expected, Forelsket made chase after them immediately.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Kokuryu
|race       = Dragon
|number     = 1498
}}

A jet-black dragon which resides at the base of Raven Falls. This dragon holds both powers of nature and harmony, and quelled any natural disasters that befell the continent of Pharm. Though it was worshipped as a deity by the people of Pharm, this dragon held a deep respect for the humans as well, allowing an amicable relationship to develop despite their differences in species. Rain, seeking the esper's power, was challenged by the dragon to test the sincerity of his words.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Gilgamesh (FFV)
|race       = Human
|number     = 1456
}}

Exdeath's guard captain who fought the Warriors of Light at Castle Exdeath located in a faraway world. He attacked Bartz and the others with what he was convinced was the legendary holy sword, which he had taken from a treasure chest within the castle. Since the sword was an imitation, he didn't stand a chance against Bartz's party and was eventually banished to the Interdimensional Rift by an indignant Exdeath.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Vlad
|race       = Demon
|number     = 1540
}}

The head of a massive monster imbued with Vlad's soul. While it is only a head, it is extremely powerful in battle, so do not let your guard down otherwise you will surely meet your demise. Destroying the crystal embedded in its forehead will halt this massive monster's activity, and one might assume that doing so will also prevent Vlad's soul from being reproduced.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Vlad
|race       = Demon
|number     = 1538
}}

The manifestation of Vlad's malice and tenacity. The vestiges of Vlad's soul that dreamt of complete and total control will not allow any existence other than its own to live. Rain and company, who were swallowed whole by a massive monster created by Vlad, witnessed a world of nothingness within the monster itself. This was the ideal world that Vlad attempted to create, and so his remnants appeared in an attempt to eradicate Rain and others who would stop him from fulfilling his vision.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Black Knight
|race       = Human
|number     = 1545
}}

A strange knight who appears in a faraway location known as the Mirage Tower. Their body is clad in black armor and they make great use of physical attacks. To enter the Mirage Tower where this black knight appears, you must receive an item that serves as a key from an ancient people who speak a certain tongue.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Stroper
|race       = Plant
|number     = 1639
}}

A plant monster that can be found below the Iifa Tree of a distant world called Gaia. The stroper usually strikes multiple targets with its sweep attack, and although originally a plant monster, it has become petrified over time. Therefore, if you use the item "soft" on it to dispel its petrification, it immediately dies, as it is unable to continue living in its currently fossilized state. Unfortunately, using a similar item in this world seems to have no such effect on it.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Rododendro
|race       = Plant
|number     = 2035
}}

A plantoid monster with poisonous red flowers and countless tentacles. Among the monsters gathered for experiments on forbidden curses, this one is particularly powerful. It is best to avoid getting too close, as it mows down anything in its path using its long tentacles in order to maintain enough space to maneuver.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Garuda
|race       = Avian
|number     = 2741
}}

A winged esper that was sealed away in the Raptor's Skydais.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Mu
|race       = Fairy
|number     = 2745
}}

A monster that inhabits the faraway world of Gaia, and was released within Lindblum for the Festival of the Hunt.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Atomos
|race       = Demon
|number     = 2769
}}

An esper of unidentifiable origin which suddenly appeared.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Diverti
|race       = Human
|number     = 2132
}}

A young man who leads the Hollow Breakers. After defeating the Will of Oblivion, Diverti began living in Visectrum and training Rinora. He ran away in a hurry when it was revealed that it was actually he who had given the pilocite to Zolulu and Delulu. Roca and her friends chased after him to retrieve the pilocite and uncover his true intentions.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Grace
|race       = Machina
|number     = 2171
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. Grace commanded the Magitek squadron when the militant Zoldaad Empire was being controlled by the mad scientist Lazarov. After being brainwashed by Lazarov, she became capable of producing magical power so strong not even she could control it. Following the nation's liberation by Rain and his allies, she seems to be devoting herself to recovering under the care of her friends.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Veritas of the Waters
|race       = Human
|number     = 2172
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. She is one of the Sworn Six of Paladia who plunged the land of Olderion into chaos. While she tormented the people with her brutal, despicable ways, it seems this was due to the split personality she developed to withstand the horrors of war. Originally a kind-hearted woman, she apparently had a deep connection to the Water Priestess and the Wardens of the Waters.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Galas
|race       = Human
|number     = 2173
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. As a member of the Orders known as the Omicron Star, he operated in the center of the Georl continent. Once a poor, weak young boy, he now lives with the sole purpose of rising to a higher position in the world. He does, however, have a hidden gentle side, having rescued and raised many abandoned dogs.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Veritas of the Dark
|race       = Human
|number     = 2174
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. As one of the Sworn Six of Paladia, he destroyed the Earth Crystal at the Earth Shrine in Grandshelt. Although his goal is to destroy all the crystals, he is somewhat of a military man, capable of showing a more rational side. He was a major reason Rain and Lasswell set off on their journey.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Hyoh
|race       = Human
|number     = 2175
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A young man known as the Delta Star of the Orders, a group of elite warriors directly under the command of the Emperor of Aldore, who rose through the ranks in record time. He always covers his face with a mask, and his true identity is unknown. His swordsmanship is so exceptional that he has even been able to master the Ultima Weapon, a great sword that long lay dormant in the treasures of Aldore's army. His abilities are unparalleled among the Orders.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Pirate
|race       = Human
|number     = 2176
}}

A pirate who trolls the seas around the Olderion Aquapolis. These unruly knaves trick travelers into hopping on their boat, at which time, once they've nowhere to run, they steal everything they have. At first they were just a band of ruffians, but under the command of a competent female pirate, they've become more like a military brigade. Even the Olderion army has been unsuccessful in putting a stop to them.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Mercedes
|race       = Human
|number     = 2177
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. The captain of a gang of pirates based in the waters of Olderion. Mercedes was born into a wealthy merchant family, but when her family's business collapsed, she lost all but a single ship and decided to become a pirate. Although she calls herself a pirate, she is also involved in vanquishing monsters in nearby waters and cracking down on those who abuse their power, so she seems to be respected by the people of the aquapolis as a rather chivalrous woman.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Ohga
|race       = Human
|number     = 2178
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A young samurai living in the Kingdom of Pharm. While Ohga typically displays a laid-back personality and a taste for elaborate clothing, when battle calls his name he is said to transform into a demon with incredible focus. He is good friends with Yuri, who is also from Pharm, and they are always skipping training together. He has developed an interest in politics since recently learning about his ancestors.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Bran
|race       = Human
|number     = 2179
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. An elf with a stern personality and a deep respect for elven traditions. After losing his brethren to the miasma in the air of Gronoa, Bran came to live in hiding in an underground castle. While he once bore resentment toward other races like any typical elf, his thinking changed after he met Ruggles the dwarf. When Bran realized that he was dying of illness like his wife, Lunera, before him, his friend Ruggles was there to take care of him in his final days and lay him to rest.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Magna
|race       = Human
|number     = 2180
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A young man who studied the ways of magic under the great mage, Mediena. Though hardworking, Magna's inflated ego often precludes him from learning from others. After Magna's magic turned Leopold into a lion, Magna was sent by Mediena on a journey to find a way to return Leopold to his human form. Along the way, Magna gained very valuable experience that helped him grow as a person.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Nagi
|race       = Human
|number     = 2181
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A member of the Orders known as the Iota Star. Seeing her beloved deceased brother, also named Hyoh, in Hyoh of the Delta Star, she will do anything he asks her to, no matter how reckless the request. Even Nagi's style of speech, which is somewhat masculine, is an imitation of her brother's. Physalis is her closest friend in the Orders.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Rizer
|race       = Human
|number     = 2182
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A young warrior who defended Grandshelt in ancient times. He is a hard worker who gained exceptional strength through steady self-discipline. Although Rizer possessed no particularly exceptional natural talents as a warrior, he fought to the very end to protect his country from its foes. His commitment to wielding his sword for his country and its people may be said to resemble the attitude of the knights of Grandshelt today.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Nameless Gunner Jake
|race       = Human
|number     = 2184
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. The former leader of the rebel group Raven, and a blood relative of the former emperor of Zoldaad. Although Jake possessed a claim to the imperial throne, he relinquished his birthright to his younger brother and went to Paladia to assist his friends in their search for Rain. Jake acts like an older brother to the party, lightening the mood and giving guidance to those with difficult decisions weighing on their minds. While the true nature of his relationship with Lid has long been ambiguous, he has finally vowed to make her happy.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Sozhe
|race       = Human
|number     = 2185
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. The former emperor of Zoldaad, and the biological father of Jake and the current emperor, Shera. He was once known as a wise but formidable man who ruled Zoldaad with great efficiency, despite its lack of natural resources. However, Lazarov took advantage of Sozhe's strong dedication to the nation and transformed Zoldaad into a dictatorship that valued rule by force. Though Sozhe died filled with regret, he was avenged through the efforts of his sons and the knights who came from Grandshelt.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Melete
|race       = Human
|number     = 2186
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A mysterious painter who worked in the Dirnado regio hundreds of years ago. Melete maneuvered her brushes with tremendous speed to produce high-quality works of art regardless of the genre. Among her many works, she is particularly famous for her paintings of airships, including "Beginning of the Dream," "The Eve Before the Flight," and "He Who Soars the Heavens." Today, it is said that no records of her existance remain aside from her signature and artwork.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Poppy
|race       = Human
|number     = 2187
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A young painter who lives in Couleur, the Kingdom of Colors. Poppy is bright and active, and wants to use her paintings to make people all over the world "happy-fied." Poppy's art is not limited only to the canvas but can also be found anywhere from the walls of abandoned houses to stones on the side of the road. Her paintings have never been appreciated by the artists living in Couleur, but they are said to have a huge following among the children living in the slums.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Lila
|race       = Human
|number     = 2188
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A female monk who has traveled across the land to master the martial arts. Abandoned as an infant in the mountains, Lila was raised by a man dubbed the "martial arts master." A naturally gifted fighter, her skills blossomed in the blink of an eye, and her intiation into the secrets of martial arts began after mastering her school's ultimate technique at a young age. She began wandering from place to place after her master, who had been like a father toher, passed away.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Zenaida
|race       = Human
|number     = 2189
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A female brawler with splendid footwork. Zenaida's superb footwork, born as a natural result of her training, captivates and defeats all who face it. Her goal is to become the world's strongest brawler, and it is said that she once rushed to an area infested by dangerous monsters in the hopes of finding and defeating her strongest opponent yet. It seems that during these fights she became able to unleash her kicks in five consecutive strikes, and her special footwork came to be known as the "Flash Kick."

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Ignacio
|race       = Human
|number     = 2190
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. The former Veritas of the Flame and one of the Sworn Six of Paladia. He is a blacksmith by trade, and created many pieces of equipment for his fellow Sworn Six members, including Raegen's weapons and Purple Lightning. Ignacio loves food and eats like a food fighter. As a result, he spends even more money in town on culinary ingredients than blacksmithing materials. Despite Ignacio's brash personality, he is something of a food snob, and his cooking skills were the best among the Sworn Six.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Wilhelm
|race       = Human
|number     = 2191
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. He was appointed as general of the Zoldaad military during the reign of the emperor, Sozhe. Wilhelm was known as the "Imperial Shield" due to the sturdiness of his shield and armor. After Zoldaad began implementing dictatorial practices, Wilhelm was removed from any crucial missions and sent to a remote location, but his love for his country never faded. When he died an untimely death, he was mourned by many, including Ludmille and Ozetta.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Forelsket
|race       = Human
|number     = 2192
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. reclusive elven chef who lived alone in an empty forest. Forelsket's cooking skills are as effective as any kind of magic, and he has spent his entire life searching for culinary ingredients. He is said to have no qualms about using any and all mysterious "ingredients" he happens to come across-grotesque monsters included.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Marie
|race       = Human
|number     = 2193
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. One of the highest-ranking mages in Mysidia today. Marie is a highly skilled user of green magic, with a brilliant mind and a wealth of knowledge at her command. She is a wonderful person, always cheerful and energetic...or so it would seem. In actuality, however, Marie is quite the eccentric. Behind her smile is said to be a calculating and logical mind that seeks to understand how much the heart of a person who has been strengthened with magic can take, as well as how low a person who has been enfeebled can fall. Sakura and Ayaka are two of the very few friends she has.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Cannon
|race       = Human
|number     = 2194
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A maid serving Sieghard's family. Cannon is able to undertake every duty in the mansion perfectly, from general household chores such as cleaning and washing to managing the lighting and effects for productions. Her skills are largely responsible for the exceptional beauty of the family's mansion even after dramatic changes that have occurred in Paladia.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Café Charlotte
|race       = Human
|number     = 2195
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A female knight who became a vision through the power of the emotions of those who gather at the Square Enix Cafe. Working in a strange land has taught Charlotte the charm of the service industry and how to smile naturally. She has also learned the art of true hospitality and matured greatly as a knight. But the most important thing Charlotte has gained is the gratitude she felt for her fellow cafe workers and the customers who visited her.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Lotti
|race       = Human
|number     = 2196
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. The granddaughter of Macmedi, a gunsmith who lives in the outskirts of Dirnado. Although Lotti inherited great magical power from her father, a black mage, she was unable to get a handle on it, and was given a custom-made magic gun by Macmedi to help her. She became very fond of Citra, who visited her shop as a customer, and from that time, her days were filled with smiles and laughter. However, her happy life was shattered by a tragic incident.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Pecciotta
|race       = Human
|number     = 2197
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A beast man who serves an organization from Paladia that works in complete secrecy. Contrary to what his adorable exterior may indicate, Pecciotta speaks in a pretty commanding voice and is quite the hard-boiled character. He is often so intense in his manner of approaching others that many who talk to him mistake him for the leader of an outlaw organization, and get quite nervous around him.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Roy
|race       = Human
|number     = 2198
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A bard who travels around the world. Ever since his sister was kidnapped by cultists, Roy has been searching for clues and gathering information by playing in taverns and on the street. During his travels, he succeeded in destroying a group of cultists with the help of Loren, the Twin Blade General of the knights of Grandshelt. In honor of Loren's valor, he composed the song "The Beautiful Twin Blade General."

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Daisy
|race       = Human
|number     = 2199
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. She is a stage actress from the Theater City of Wohlstock. With high-level acting skills and the versatility needed to play a wide array of roles, Daisy has been well received by audiences. Despite being a newcomer, she was chosen to play the role of the Shield in "Of Swords and Shields," which shot her into stardom. Later, she accompanied Fina and her friends after they brought back the emotions stolen from Wohlstock by the Hollow. During the journey, she and Fina become close friends.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Blossom Sage Sakura
|race       = Human
|number     = 2200
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A woman who was Veritas of the Bolt and one of the Sworn Six of Paladia. Although Sakura appears young, she is truly over seven hundred years old. Possessing incredible knowledge and magic power, it seems she was known as the "Sage of Mysidia" in the magical nation. When Rain and Sol went missing, she felt deeply responsible for their disappearance and worked hard to solve the mystery of the gate's mechanism.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Maritime Strategist Nichol
|race       = Human
|number     = 2201
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A strategist for the Olderion Federation. Nichol is one of the Wardens of the Waters and the brother of Elle and Luka. Though his emphasis on calm, rational thinking may make it seem as though he takes his family for granted, deep down, he truly cares for his brother and sister. Since journeying to Paladia, he has started wearing the glasses that were prepared by Elle and given to him by Arsha as a birthday present.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Sieghard
|race       = Human
|number     = 2202
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A man who was Veritas of the Earth and one of the Sworn Six of Paladia. Sieghard loves poetry, painting, fighting, and, above all, beauty, judging all things based on whether or not they are beautiful. He was brought up to value beauty, with the big-hearted and flamboyant Theobald as his older brother and the strong-willed and confident Dietlinde as his older sister. He was flabbergasted at being outshined by Dark Fina and has viewed her as his rival ever since.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Citra
|race       = Human
|number     = 2203
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A woman who was Veritas of the Light and one of the Sworn Six of Paladia. While Citra is strict with herself and others, seven hundred years ago in Paladia, she was a sisterly figure who cared for Sakura more than anyone else in the world. In addition to her magical attacks, she also has the ability to fight with the help of espers and is quite skilled as a summoner.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Hess King Lasswell
|race       = Human
|number     = 2204
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A knight of Grandshelt and the king of Hess. Lasswell had long been dependent on his dear friend since childhood, Rain, but with the help of good mentors and friends, he grew into a man worthy of becoming the king of Hess. While he is now busy with his political duties as king, he sometimes recalls the days he spent with his mentors and friends. His most treasured possession is his beloved sword, Purple Lightning, which he cherishes so much that he never lets it leave his side.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Bruce
|race       = Human
|number     = 2206
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A calm, mature passenger on the Farplane Express. Bruce is a master of card tricks, helped by his highly dexterous fingers. During his travels with Fina, he takes an active role in caring for Roca, showing himself to be perfectly capable of managing everything from the changing of diapers to the sewing of bibs. He met his wife through his magic tricks and apparently taught his own child magic tricks with great enthusiasm. He seems to have at one time been a summoner, but little else is known about his past.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Madam Edel
|race       = Human
|number     = 2207
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. The master of a manor located in an unexplored region of Crystallis. It seems she is using a secretive organization from Paladia known as "Morze's Soiree" to achieve a certain goal. Possessing a captivating charm, she is adored by the Soiree's members, who call her "Madam." Her love of drinking is second only to her love of adventure and treasure

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Veritas of the Dark
|race       = Human
|number     = 2635
}}

A man clad in the Darklord's armor. He appears before Raegen after abducting Rain in Lapis. Although he seems to know Raegen, his identity and goals are hidden beneath the darkness of his helm.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = White Lily Dark Fina
|race       = Human
|number     = 2208
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. One of the Eight Sages of Hess, she was sealed in a crystal for hundreds of years. Dark Fina possessed incredible magical power and strength beyond human comprehension, and she has saved Rain and his friends many times. During the war with Aldore, she was feared for her overwhelming magical power and was apparently known as "Hess's strongest warrior."

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Sol
|race       = Human
|number     = 2209
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. One of the Eight Sages of Hess, he was sealed in a crystal for hundreds of years. During that time, he was tainted by the evil will of humans, causing him to hate all forms of life. He tried to destroy Lapis by summoning Chaotic Darkness, but he failed due to the efforts of Rain and his friends. Sol then used the gate's power to jump into Paladia. He has an obsession with the sun, which he often likens to Rain's supposed hypocrisy.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Sol
|race       = Human
|number     = 2151
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. One of the Eight Sages of Hess, he was sealed in a crystal for hundreds of years. During that time, he was tainted by the evil will of humans, causing him to hate all forms of life. He tried to destroy Lapis by summoning Chaotic Darkness, but he failed due to the efforts of Rain and his friends. Sol then used the gate's power to jump into Paladia. He has an obsession with the sun, which he often likens to Rain's supposed hypocrisy.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Awakened Dragon Akstar
|race       = Human
|number     = 2210
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A master swordsman who was formerly Zeno of the Beta Star. Circumstances bade that Akstar slumber within a crystal, but he awoke after the war in Paladia came to a close. After learning the Mirror of Equity from Lasswell, he created a new version of his own called the Guiding Mirror of Equity. An exceptionally gifted swordsman, Akstar continues to push the limits of his own skills.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Cleome
|race       = Human
|number     = 2211
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A girl from Symphonia, the Scholastic City. Cleome is a musical prodigy who can play any instrument with very little practice. Despite her quiet and gentle nature, she shows even greater talent with blades than she does with musical instruments. If, like Lasswell, she is able to study under a skilled mentor, she has the potential to become a truly great blademaster. As an admirer of Akstar's swordsmanship, she has begun following him to learn the technique and attitude of a swordsman.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Aldore King Rain
|race       = Human
|number     = 2212
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. He is a knight of Grandshelt and the king of Aldore. He and Lasswell overcame their clashing blood to save the people of Paladia from suffering under the oppression of Emperor Vlad. Since defeating Vlad and restoring peace, Rain devotes himself to state affairs. He has the support of his friends, and his many achievements make him a worthy king, even if he himself remains unaccustomed to the title. Rain keeps his trusty sword, the Crimson Saber, by his side at all times.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Blue Mage Fina
|race       = Human
|number     = 2213
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. A girl who was guided by a mysterious voice and awakened to her power as a blue mage. She has great admiration for Dark Fina, another version of herself, as well as her fellow travelers Rain and Lasswell, and works hard every day to be worthy of standing alongside them. That strong desire, along with her experiences traveling on the Farplane Express and making new friends, has truly helped Fina grow.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Gluttony
|race       = Human
|number     = 2254
}}

One of the seven Homunculus serving under the man they call "Father" who appears in tales of a faraway world where alchemy is practiced. Gluttony is always hungry, and will eat anything or anyone to satisfy his appetite. When angered, his upper body splits open, revealing an opening that resembles a grotesque mouth. The white bone-like spikes protruding from torso are said to be capable of swallowing anything in an instant.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Raegen
|race       = Human
|number     = 2205
}}

A vision that emerged from a crystal. He is the father of Rain and Lasswell, and was once known as Veritas of the Dark. He strived to convince the Eight Sages of Hess, including Dark Fina and Rowen, to support his efforts in building a new era. After the schemes of Aldore's emperor resulted in Raegen being banished to Lapis, he resolved to live for his friends and family, and served as a knight of Grandshelt. He now devotes himself to supporting his newly crowned sons.

{{Monster Infobox
|name       = Darkpede
|race       = Insect
|number     = 1627
}}

